                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78ef5dab-b5eb-36bd-97c3-7c6ed3a3b1f3",
                        "entry_id": "5ff42c37-0242-3369-af1a-8c9e804ad501",
                        "glosses": [
                            "доходить до тонкости, до виртуозности в чем-нибудь, делать что-либо мастерски"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e11f9a9c-d519-4ef7-9b55-f00891fb2f21",
                                "sense_id": "78ef5dab-b5eb-36bd-97c3-7c6ed3a3b1f3",
                                "text": "Изощряться в любезностях."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0385b339-d529-41e1-adf1-ab074c04c913",
                                "sense_id": "78ef5dab-b5eb-36bd-97c3-7c6ed3a3b1f3",
                                "text": "Через два-три дня старший лейтенант стал общим любимцем, и бригады изощрялись в выдумывании предлогов, чтобы только заполучить его для работы в свой состав."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7fefec8f-213c-3e7a-ab25-805ae501bf62",
                        "entry_id": "5ff42c37-0242-3369-af1a-8c9e804ad501",
                        "glosses": [
                            "становиться более восприимчивым, острым (о слухе, внимании)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d1194c9-b094-44aa-a791-9e0e9dae595c",
                                "sense_id": "7fefec8f-213c-3e7a-ab25-805ae501bf62",
                                "text": "Всякий поймет, однако, что собственно мышечному чувству дана способность анализировать свои ощущения только во времени, да и эта способность, как сейчас увидим, изощряется лишь при помощи слуха, зрения и частого упражнения мышц, т. е. приобретается заучением."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b09877f3-3b41-4dc2-918a-1b7299846cbc",
                                "sense_id": "7fefec8f-213c-3e7a-ab25-805ae501bf62",
                                "text": "С детства воспитывались и изощрялись в нём чувство и ум."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6eda7902-dda9-4824-b9f4-ff00ca111e9c",
                                "sense_id": "7fefec8f-213c-3e7a-ab25-805ae501bf62",
                                "text": "Оттого ли, что он вращался среди художников, изощрилось в нём пластическое чувство, или оттого он любил дружить с художниками, что в нём оно било ключом, но это общение и эта способность сделали Аретино первым художественным критиком, настоящим создателем этого вида литературы, который именно и должен был возникнуть в дни золотого заката Возрождения, когда живопись взлетала на вершины человеческих достижений…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1b135c56-dfdb-4e66-a49d-d8b1707d9024",
                        "source_entry_id": "5ff42c37-0242-3369-af1a-8c9e804ad501",
                        "source_sense_description": "мастерски делать что-либо",
                        "target_lang_word": "acquire refinement",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cbe2589f-65c8-4991-95f3-7337d2598986",
                        "source_entry_id": "5ff42c37-0242-3369-af1a-8c9e804ad501",
                        "source_sense_description": "мастерски делать что-либо",
                        "target_lang_word": "excel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "excel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5ba8d0a-01fa-3854-a0fd-82e70ccd9cea",
                                        "entry_id": "c6358ea2-8fd4-3c26-be97-d0379acbeb02",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To surpass someone or something; to be better or do better than someone or something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "312ebf57-0e51-4b27-88ad-4536518cb23c",
                                                "sense_id": "f5ba8d0a-01fa-3854-a0fd-82e70ccd9cea",
                                                "text": "I excelled everyone else with my exam results."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "830fd6ec-c272-48f2-a857-07df49ef9117",
                                                "sense_id": "f5ba8d0a-01fa-3854-a0fd-82e70ccd9cea",
                                                "text": "La Rochefoucauld, the French philosopher, said: \"If you want enemies, excel your friends; but if you want friends, let your friends excel you.\" Why is that true? Because when our friends excel us, that gives them a feeling of importance; but when we excel them, that gives them a feeling of inferiority and arouses envy and jealousy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc0b793e-e7d9-380e-bb11-8374ba710efd",
                                        "entry_id": "c6358ea2-8fd4-3c26-be97-d0379acbeb02",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be much better than others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a727b6cd-d599-4ee3-9716-19efa786134a",
                                                "sense_id": "dc0b793e-e7d9-380e-bb11-8374ba710efd",
                                                "text": "But it is as a destroyer of grasshoppers that the dickcissel excels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "993df415-e1c9-4dc3-ae91-dbeb0abbbe7a",
                                                "sense_id": "dc0b793e-e7d9-380e-bb11-8374ba710efd",
                                                "text": "1924: Aristotle, Metaphysics. Translated by W. D. Ross. Nashotah, Wisconsin, USA: The Classical Library, 2001. Book 1, Part 2..\nIf, then, there is something in what the poets say, and jealousy is natural to the divine power, it would probably occur in this case above all, and all who excelled in this knowledge would be unfortunate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3e77ebb-f5a1-4569-9d01-1c2b0238f49d",
                                                "sense_id": "dc0b793e-e7d9-380e-bb11-8374ba710efd",
                                                "text": "Lescott gave his finest England performance alongside his former Everton team-mate Phil Jagielka, who also excelled despite playing with a fractured toe, while Parker was given a deserved standing ovation when he was substituted late on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4aefbcc8-8cce-485d-922d-369667155072",
                                                "sense_id": "dc0b793e-e7d9-380e-bb11-8374ba710efd",
                                                "text": "From Rosie the Riveter to Coco Channel^([sic – meaning Coco Chanel]) (in pants!), from Amelia Earhart to the quaintrelle (the female dandy), change in women's dress has symbolized everything from the right and need to work outside the home to wearing pants as a fashion statement to excelling at a profession (even as an aviatrix) to once again claiming the right to cultivate life's pleasures."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71e29386-0730-39e3-a5c6-380205a337ae",
                                        "entry_id": "c6358ea2-8fd4-3c26-be97-d0379acbeb02",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To exceed, to go beyond."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "936299ef-8be8-43bb-90b1-91d98f0c3ed6",
                                                "sense_id": "71e29386-0730-39e3-a5c6-380205a337ae",
                                                "text": "She opened; but to shut / Excelled her power: the gates wide open stood […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a841103-33c5-456e-be75-1c401200ca02",
                                                "sense_id": "71e29386-0730-39e3-a5c6-380205a337ae",
                                                "text": "I reason, we could die : / The best vitality / Cannot excel decay; / But what of that?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
